    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0752" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.404/10–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-10">October 10,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received October 9 [<hi rendition="#italic">10?</hi>]—9:38
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Press here carries sensational accounts of Vincent’s broadcast (ZA 6688)
                    October 7<anchor n="28" xml:id="d525-f1"/> in regard to abolition of Shintoism
                    as Japanese state religion. GHQ Information and Education Section is receiving
                    numerous inquiries as to details, etc., and it would be helpful if pertinent
                    information could be sent us by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d525-f1" n="28" xml:id="d525-f1-content">
                <p>For text of radio broadcast, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, October 7, 1945, pp. 538–545.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
